// Copyright (c) 2026, the Flutter Agent Harness authors.
// Use of this source code is governed by a MIT license that can be found
// in the LICENSE file.

import 'dart:io';

import 'package:flutter/foundation.dart';
import 'package:flutter/services.dart';

import 'package:fa/services/app_log.dart';

/// Marks paths excluded from cloud device backups.
///
/// gh-1730 review: the mobile sandbox's `.dap` hub tree holds the hub
/// `clientSecret` (accepted directly as a credential), the agent identity
/// key, and X25519 channel keypairs. On iOS `getApplicationDocumentsDirectory()`
/// is `Documents/`, which the default iCloud device backup includes — the
/// same class of leak issue #329 E4 stopped for `fah_keychain.xml`. The
/// native side (`fah/icloud` `excludeFromBackup`, AppDelegate.swift) sets
/// `NSURLIsExcludedFromBackupKey` on the subtree; Android needs no call
/// (its `app_flutter` documents dir already sits outside the default Auto
/// Backup domains, per the #329 E4 audit).
const MethodChannel _icloudChannel = MethodChannel('fah/icloud');

/// Test seam: replaces the platform call entirely (unit tests record the
/// requested path instead of round-tripping a channel no host implements).
@visibleForTesting
Future<void> Function(String path)? excludePathFromBackupOverride;

/// Marks the file or directory at [path] excluded from cloud backups.
///
/// A failure must never break boot — the exclusion is hardening, not a
/// precondition — so every error path logs and moves on.
Future<void> excludePathFromBackup(String path) async {
  final override = excludePathFromBackupOverride;
  if (override != null) {
    await override(path);
    return;
  }
  if (!Platform.isIOS) return;
  try {
    await _icloudChannel.invokeMethod<void>('excludeFromBackup', {
      'path': path,
    });
  } on MissingPluginException {
    // No native handler (unit tests, macOS) — nothing to exclude with.
  } on PlatformException catch (e) {
    AppLog.i('sandbox', 'backup exclusion failed for $path: ${e.message}');
  }
}

blocks.text:
There's a `fah/icloud` channel handling iCloud container. I'll add an `excludeFromBackup` method to it — semantically the right home (iCloud backup policy). The Swift side:

```swift
case "excludeFromBackup":
 let args = call.arguments as? [String: Any] ?? [:]
 guard let path = args["path"] as? String, !path.isEmpty else {
   result(FlutterError(code: "bad_args", message: "path is required", details: nil))
   return
 }
 result(iCloudExcludeFromBackup(path))
``

and

```swift
/// Marks the file/directory at [path] excluded from iCloud device backups
/// (NSURLIsExcludedFromBackupKey). ... For directories the flag excludes the
/// whole subtree ...
private func iCloudExcludeFromBackup(_ path: String) -> Any {
 var url = URL(fileURLWithPath: path)
 // hmm, need do/catch
 do {
   var resourceValues = URLResourceValues()
   resourceValues.isExcludedFromBackup = true
   var mutableUrl = url
   try mutableUrl.setResourceValues(resourceValues)
   // verify?
   return true
 } catch {
   return FlutterError(code: "exclude_failed", ...)
 }
``

Note: `setResourceValues` requires `var` on the URL. The standard pattern:

```swift
let url = URL(fileURLWithPath: path)
var resourceValues = URLResourceValues()
resourceValues.isExcludedFromBackup = true
var mutableUrl = url
try mutableUrl.setResourceValues(resourceValues)
``

One important nuance: the flag should also be re-aplied to contents. Apple docs (QA1719): "If your application creates a folder... you can exclude the folder from backup by setting the attribute on the folder itself" — for folders, the backup exclusion applies to the folder; files created INSIDE an excluded folder are also excluded at backup time? Actually QA1719 says: "you can set this attribute on a directory to exclude the directory and its contents"... Let me be careful. The commonly cited doc: https://developer.apple.com/library/archive/qa/qa1719/_index.html "Technical Q&A QA1719 — How do I prevent files from being backed up to iCloud and iTunes?" It says: "Set the NSURLIsExcludedFromBackupKey on the file... For a directory, setting the attribute excludes the directory and all its contents" — I recall QA1719's option is about `NSURLIsExcludedFromBackupKey` for individual files AND there's a note that new files created in an excluded directory do NOT automatically inherit the flag?? Hmm.

Let me recall precisely. QA1719 lists:
1. Files that are restorable → Caches/ or tmp.
2. `NSURLIsExcludedFromBackupKey` — "iOS 5.1 and later ... the file will not be backed up"; "this attribute can be set on a directory to exclude it and its contents" — I'm fairly confident modern behavior: the backup daemon skips the entire subtree when the directory has the flag. There are many StackOverflow answers confirming directory-level exclusion covers contents (that's how apps exclude whole caches dirs).

But some sources note: the attribute must be applied to each file for app-level "do not back up"... The official doc for `isExcludedFromBackup`: "Setting this value to true on a directory excludes the directory and everything inside it from backups." Actually — Apple's documentation for URLResourceKey.isExcludedFromBackupKey states: "If the value is true, the resource is not backed up... For directories, all contents are also excluded." I'll go with directory-level exclusion on `.dap` — that's exactly what the review thread suggests ("set the NSURLIsExcludedFromBackupKey URL resource key on the sandbox .dap subtree").

To be extra safe (the reviewer says "subtree"), I can also walk existing children and set the flag on each — cheap at creation time (the dir is fresh/empty at that point, but a pre-existing install upgrading would have content). I'll implement: set on the directory + recursively on existing descendants. That covers the upgrade path where `.dap` already has keys/config from the previous app version.

Dart side: in env_factory_io.dart, after creating sandbox, create `<sandbox>/.dap` and call the exclusion service on iOS. Where to put the Dart wrapper? A new file `flutter_app/lib/services/backup_exclusion.dart` (+ `_io`/`_stub` variants? The channel call is iOS-only). Look at how icloud_sync_service_io vs stub are structured, and how env_factory_io would import it. Actually simpler: one small file `backup_exclusion.dart` with `Future<void> excludeFromBackups(String path)` that:
- no-ops unless Platform.isIOS
- invokes MethodChannel('fah/icloud').invokeMethod('excludeFromBackup', {'path': path})
